[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2830566868","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105746#issuecomment-2830566868","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105746","id":2830566868,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6otwXU","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-25T14:18:46Z","updated_at":"2025-04-25T14:33:24Z","body":"> This means that the underlying collision detection during simulation really only needs exactly one contact per shape, and that contact can be anywhere, which means we can set Jolt's underlying collision collector to be the much cheaper `JPH::AnyHitCollisionCollector` for any collision involving sensors/areas.\r\n\r\nIt's probably worth linking [this specific comment](https://github.com/jrouwe/JoltPhysics/discussions/1476#discussioncomment-12025632) as well, to highlight one compromise of this `CollideShapeVsShapePerLeaf<AnyHitCollisionCollector<...>>` helper, which is the heap allocation that it incurs when either of the two bodies overlap by more than 32 of its shapes.\r\n\r\nNote however (as mentioned there) that Jolt caches collision results inbetween physics steps if the two objects haven't moved by more than a certain amount relative to eachother, so you'll only end up paying this cost when you have an `Area3D` actually moving around during such overlaps.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2830566868/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831187068","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105746#issuecomment-2831187068","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105746","id":2831187068,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6owHx8","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-25T18:54:06Z","updated_at":"2025-04-25T18:54:06Z","body":"Change looks good.\r\n\r\nReminder to update https://github.com/godotengine/godot-docs/blob/master/tutorials/physics/using_jolt_physics.rst\r\n\r\nAlso there is one gotcha: In the case of an area colliding with a mesh shape, you might receive a hit for a different triangle if the area or body moves. This results in a different `SubShapeID`. This would trigger a `ContactListener::OnContactAdded` for the new ID followed by a  `ContactListener::OnContactRemoved` for the old ID. I think you handle this case in `JoltContactListener3D::_flush_area_shifts` but I'm mentioning it just in case.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831187068/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2836767242","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105746#issuecomment-2836767242","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105746","id":2836767242,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6pFaIK","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-28T21:31:31Z","updated_at":"2025-04-28T21:31:48Z","body":"> Also there is one gotcha: In the case of an area colliding with a mesh shape, you might receive a hit for a different triangle if the area or body moves. This results in a different `SubShapeID`. This would trigger a `ContactListener::OnContactAdded` for the new ID followed by a `ContactListener::OnContactRemoved` for the old ID. I think you handle this case in `JoltContactListener3D::_flush_area_shifts` but I'm mentioning it just in case.\r\n\r\nIt's good that you bring this up actually. I had forgotten to apply [the fix](https://github.com/jrouwe/JoltPhysics/discussions/1476#discussioncomment-11955014) that I had in mind for this, but now that I'm actually testing it out I'm seeing some odd results that I think stem from this breaking some fundamental assumptions made by `_flush_area_shifts`.\r\n\r\nI'm gonna set this PR to draft for now and do some more testing at a later point.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2836767242/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2918861179","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105746#issuecomment-2918861179","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105746","id":2918861179,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6t-kl7","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-29T09:39:30Z","updated_at":"2025-05-29T09:40:01Z","body":"Rebased and added the forcing of `JPH::EBackFaceMode::CollideWithBackFaces` for sensor collisions, as suggested [here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106629#issuecomment-2905560451).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2918861179/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2918913803","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105746#issuecomment-2918913803","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105746","id":2918913803,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6t-xcL","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-29T10:02:16Z","updated_at":"2025-05-29T10:02:16Z","body":"I guess I should also give an update here to say that merging #106918 should allow this to be merged afterwards, as it seems to resolve the \"odd results\" I mentioned above.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2918913803/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2934084437","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105746#issuecomment-2934084437","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105746","id":2934084437,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6u4pNV","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-03T08:20:08Z","updated_at":"2025-06-03T13:50:31Z","body":"I threw in another rebase for good measure.\r\n\r\nNow that #106918 has been merged, this should be ready to go.\r\n\r\nIf you want some hard numbers, here's some quick before-and-after profiling using the built-in \"Physics Process\" monitor, in [this scene](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20564929/area-vs-concave.zip), where a cylinder-shaped Area3D goes in and out of overlap with a ConcavePolygonShape3D consisting of around 1000 triangles:\r\n\r\n![Before](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5c8225f7-7f2a-48c6-bda4-ca35a98e5ae2)\r\n![After](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e277f78b-227d-419c-8570-f9f63917681e)\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2934084437/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2934116973","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105746#issuecomment-2934116973","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105746","id":2934116973,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6u4xJt","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_